. San Francisco traded first- and fourth-round selections (27th and 138th overall) to Miami in exchange for first- and third-round selections (30th and 90th overall). \u2191 No. 28: Houston \u2192 Buffalo \u2192 New England. Multiple trades: Houston \u2192 Buffalo (D). See Round 1: Buffalo \u2192 Houston . Buffalo \u2192 New England (D). Buffalo traded a first-round selection (28th overall) to New England in exchange for first- and fourth-round selections (31st and 125th overall). \u2191 No. 29: LA Rams \u2192 Kansas City (PD). The LA Rams traded first-, fifth- and sixth-round selections (29th, 169th and 210th overall), and a 2027 third-round selection to Kansas City in exchange for CB Trent McDuffie . \u2191 No. 30: Denver \u2192 Miami \u2192 San Francisco \u2192 NY Jets. Multiple trades: Denver \u2192 Miami (PD). Denver traded first-, third- and fourth-round selections (30th, 94th and 130th overall) to Miami in exchange for a fourth-round selection (111th overall) and WR Jaylen Waddle . Miami \u2192 San Francisco (D). See Round 1: San Francisco \u2192 Miami . San Francisco \u2192 NY Jets (D). San Francisco traded a first-round selection (30th overall) to the NY Jets in exchange for second- and fifth-round selections (33rd and 179th overall). \u2191 No. 31: New England \u2192 Buffalo \u2192 Tennessee. Multiple trades: New England \u2192 Buffalo (D). See Round 1: Buffalo \u2192 New England . Buffalo \u2192 Tennessee (D). Buffalo traded first-, third- and fifth-round selections (31st, 69th and 165th overall) to Tennessee in exchange for second-, third- and fourth-round selections (35th, 66th and 101st overall). Round 2 [ edit ] \u2191 No. 33: NY Jets \u2192 San Francisco (D). See Round 1: San Francisco \u2192 NY Jets . \u2191 No. 35: Tennessee \u2192 Buffalo (D). See Round 1: Buffalo \u2192 Tennessee . \u2191 No. 36: Las Vegas \u2192 Houston (D). Las Vegas traded second- and fourth-round selections (36th and 117th overall) to Houston in exchange for second- and third