ennessee Titans Nick Westbrook-Ikhine WR Indiana Trades within the draft [ edit ] (PD) indicates trades completed prior to the start of the draft (i.e. P re- D raft), while (D) denotes trades which took place during the 2020 draft. Round 1 ^ No. 13: Multiple trades: Indianapolis \u2192 San Francisco (PD). Indianapolis traded a first-round selection (13th overall) to San Francisco in exchange for DT DeForest Buckner . San Francisco \u2192 Tampa Bay (D). San Francisco traded first- and seventh-round selections (13th and 245th overall ) to Tampa Bay in exchange for first- and fourth-round selections ( 14th and 117th overall ). ^ No. 14: Tampa Bay \u2192 San Francisco (D). See Round 1: San Francisco \u2192 Tampa Bay . ^ No. 18: Pittsburgh \u2192 Miami (PD). Pittsburgh traded first- and fifth-round selections (18th and 154th overall ) and a 2021 sixth-round selection to Miami in exchange for a fourth-round selection ( 135th overall ) and S Minkah Fitzpatrick . ^ No. 19: Chicago \u2192 Las Vegas (PD). Chicago traded first- and third-round selections (19th and 81st overall ), and 2019 first- and sixth-round selections to Las Vegas in exchange for a second-round selection and a conditional seventh-round selection ( 43rd and 226th overall ), and LB Khalil Mack ; the seventh-round selection could have become a fifth-round selection if conditions had been met. ^ No. 20: LA Rams \u2192 Jacksonville (PD). The LA Rams traded a first-round selection (20th overall), and 2021 first- and fourth-round selections to Jacksonville in exchange for CB Jalen Ramsey . ^ No. 22: Buffalo \u2192 Minnesota (PD). Buffalo traded first-, fifth- and sixth-round selections (22nd, 155th and 201st overall ), and a 2021 fourth-round selection to Minnesota in exchange for a seventh-round selection ( 239th overall ) and WR Stefon Diggs . ^ No. 23: New England \u2192 LA Chargers (D). New England traded a first-round selection (23rd overall) to the LA Chargers in exchange for second- and third-round selections ( 37th and 71st overall ). ^ No. 25: Minnesota \u2192 San Francisco (D). Minnesota traded a first-round selection (25th overall) to San Francisco in exchange for first-, fourth- and fifth-round selections ( 31st , 117th and 176th overall ). ^ No. 26: Multiple trades: Houston \u2192 Miami (PD). Houston traded a first-round selection (26th overall), 2021 first- and second-round selections, OT Juli\u00e9n Davenport and CB Johnson Bademosi to Miami in exchange for a fourth-round selection ( 111th overall ), a 2021 sixth-round selection, WR Kenny Stills and OT Laremy Tunsil . Miami \u2192 Green Bay (D). Miami traded a first-round selection (26th overall) to Green Bay in exchange for first- and fourth-round selections ( 30th and 136th overall ). ^ No. 30: Green Bay \u2192 Miami (D). See Round 1: Miami \u2192 Green Bay . ^ No. 31: San Francisco \u2192 Minnesota (D). See Round 1: Minnesota \u2192 San Francisco . Round 2 ^ No. 34: Washington \u2192 Indianapolis (PD). Washington traded a second-round selection (34th overall) and a 2019 second-round selection to Indianapolis in exchange for a 2019 first-round selection. ^ No. 37: LA Chargers \u2192 New England (D). See Round 1: New England \u2192 LA Chargers . ^ No. 40: Arizona \u2192 Houston (PD). Arizona traded a second-round selection (40th overall), a 2021 fourth-round selection and RB David Johnson to Houston in exchange for a fourth-round selection and WR DeAndre Hopkins . ^ No. 41: Cleveland \u2192 Indianapolis (D). Cleveland traded a second-round selection ( 41st overall ) to Indianapolis in exchange for second- and fifth-round selections ( 44th and 160th overall ). ^ No. 43: Las Vegas \u2192 Chicago (PD). See Round 1: Chicago \u2192 Las Vegas . ^ No. 44: Indianapolis \u2192 Cleveland (D). See Round 2: Cleveland \u2192 Indianapolis . ^ No. 41: NY Jets \u2192 Seattle (D). The NY Jets traded a second-round selection ( 48th overall ) to Seattle in exchange for second- and third-round selections ( 59th and 101st overal