ith Ex-Rep. Ben 'Cooter' Jones Archived June 28, 2015, at the Wayback Machine on YouTube \u2191 Ben Jones tells CNN why the Confederate flag should be on license plates Archived January 13, 2016, at the Wayback Machine on YouTube \u2191 \"The NAACP on Confederate Symbols\" . NAACP . Archived from the original on August 22, 2019 . Retrieved August 22, 2019 . \u2191 \"Dukes of Hazzard star Ben Jones defends Confederate flag, attributes backlash to political correctness\" . New York Daily News . Archived from the original on August 22, 2019 . Retrieved August 22, 2019 . \u2191 Rifkin, Glenn (August 10, 2026). \"Ben Jones, 'Dukes of Hazzard' Actor and Congressman, Dies at 84\" . The New York Times . Retrieved August 10, 2026 . \u2191 Dunn, Jack (August 9, 2026). \"Ben Jones, Actor Turned Politician Who Played Cooter Davenport in 'The Dukes of Hazzard,' Dies at 84\" . Variety . Archived from the original on August 10, 2026 . Retrieved August 10, 2026 . External links [ edit ] Appearances on C-SPAN Ben Jones at IMDb Ben Jones discography at Discogs Biography at the Biographical Directory of the United States Congress Financial information (federal office) at the Federal Election Commission Campaign contributions for 2002 U.S. Congressional District 7 of Virginia Welcome to Cooters place, Gatlinburg, Tennessee and Nashville, Tennessee The Dukes of Hazzard star who could destroy Newt Gingrich... again , Ed Pilkington, The Guardian , January 26, 2011 U.S. House of Representatives Preceded by Pat Swindall Member of the U.S. House of Representatives from Georgia's 4th congressional district 1989\u20131993 Succeeded by John Linder v t e The Dukes of Hazzard Episodes Characters Bo Duke Luke Duke Daisy Duke Sheriff Rosco P. Coltrane Boss Hogg Television films Reunion! (1997) Hazzard in Hollywood (2000) Remake films The Dukes of Hazzard (2005) soundtrack The Beginning (2007) Video games The Dukes of Hazzard Racing for Home Daisy Dukes It Out Return of the General Lee Hazard Run Sp